(A Bare Act is the primary legislation enacted by Parliament or a State Legislature that establishes legally binding) Tj
T* (rules. The actor is the Legislature, which creates the law, while courts, government authorities, and citizens interpret,) Tj
T* (administer, and comply with its provisions. The legal effect is the creation of enforceable rights, duties, powers,) Tj
T* (liabilities, and penalties that have legal force. The structural purpose of this concept is to provide the statutory) Tj
T* (foundation of the legal framework before detailed provisions, procedures, and enforcement mechanisms are) Tj
T* (introduced. My key drafting choice was to use precise legal terminology such as "enacted," "legally binding," and) Tj
T* ("enforceable" instead of policy-oriented or descriptive language. This ensures the provision communicates) Tj
